hadiths[2]{hadithnumber,text}:
"958","Yahya related to me from Malik from Nafi that Abdullah ibn Umarused to stop for a long time at the first two jamras saying, ""Allah isgreater"", ""Glory be to Allah"", ""Praise be to Allah"", and making duasto Allah, but he did not stop at the jamrat al-Aqaba."
"1090","Yahya related to me from Malik from Zayd ibn Aslam from Ata ibnYasar that a man from the Ansar of the tribe of Banu Haritha washerding a pregnant she-camel at Uhud. It was about to die, so heslaughtered it with a sharp stake. The Messenger of Allah was askedabout that, and he said, ""There is no harm in it, eat it."
